OL,24,ANext Page BNW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,365,360,120,260,000,100
PN,36403
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F364A1786605488
OL,3,CAlmost 500 children injured in e-
OL,4,Cscooter incidents since 2019, study
OL,5,Cfinds
OL,7,FBetween January 2019 and December
OL,8,F2024, three children's trauma centres
OL,9,Frecorded 477 patients with e-scooter
OL,10,Finjuries.
OL,12,FAlmost three quarters (74%) lived in
OL,13,Fthe most deprived areas.
OL,15,FThe average age of the injured
OL,16,Fchildren was 12, and half were aged
OL,17,Fbetween 10 and 13.
OL,19,FMost injuries, 95%, were sustained by
OL,20,Fthe rider, and 80% of incidents
OL,21,Finvolved private e-scooters.
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G3/8
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,365,360,120,260,000,100
PN,36404
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F364A1786605488
OL,3,CAlmost 500 children injured in e-
OL,4,Cscooter incidents since 2019, study
OL,5,Cfinds
OL,7,FJust 2.5% of injuries happened on
OL,8,Fprivate land.
OL,10,FThe most common injuries were to the
OL,11,Farms and legs, but almost a quarter
OL,12,F(24.1%) were head injuries.
OL,14,FOne in 10 head injuries were severe
OL,15,Fenough to require scans, hospital
OL,16,Fadmission and surgery in some cases.
OL,18,FOf the most seriously injured
OL,19,Fchildren, almost half (48%) were hurt
OL,20,Fafter colliding with a car or
OL,21,Fstationary object.
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G4/8
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
